  "name": "Dynamic Contrast — Photographic Detail",
  "description": "Three-band photographic local contrast with smooth-radius, two-ring neighbourhood sampling. Fine Detail changes one-pixel microcontrast; Medium Texture emphasizes surface structure; Large Structure shapes broader depth. Texture Radius sets the outer medium-band sampling radius in source pixels; the large-band radius is four times larger. Shadow/Highlight Protect progressively attenuate detail near tonal endpoints, Midtone Focus prioritizes midtones, Halo Limit caps per-channel correction, and Color Guard reduces enhancement on highly saturated pixels. Effect Mix adjusts overall intensity. Negative Detail values soften their band. Use for landscape, architecture and natural textures; moderate Large Structure to minimize wide edge halos. This is a single-pass approximation using sparse neighbourhood samples, not a true edge-aware Gaussian pyramid or RAW highlight recovery.",
